{# viz_compare (COMPARISON family of the data-viz PRESET layer): formula_ladder,
   grouped_bars, stacked_bar_100, entity_bars. These are the devices the owner
   refs use to COMPARE quantities: a calculation derived step by step, a
   before/after per category, a composition of a whole, and entities ranked on
   one metric.

   Brand-agnostic / token-only: every colour arrives as var(--token) + color-mix
   from styles/viz_compare.css; no hex, no font-family literal, no branding.
   Macros take (v, uid=0): uid (the dispatch's loop.index) keeps every DOM id
   page-unique so two equal-valued devices never collide.

   The verbatim law: every figure is printed EXACTLY as the writer supplied it
   ("3-5", "1.200", "2,5", "13.160 €"). Only the bar GEOMETRY is derived, via the
   `num` filter (German convention: thousands dot, decimal comma), so a width can
   never diverge from the numeral above it, and a range never collapses into a
   single fabricated number. Graceful: a missing required field renders NOTHING,
   so adding a spec to a page can never break a render. Nothing is invented: no
   figure, no source, no segment, no legend text.

   These are HTML/CSS box devices (like split_bar / ranked_bars), not SVG: widths
   are percentages of the host column, so they reflow inside any Chromium print
   column and can never blow a fixed mm height. #}

{# formula_ladder (the CALCULATION device). A vertical ladder of numbered steps,
   each a hairline-separated row of: accent numeral chip, the BIG value, its unit,
   and the explanatory label. The ladder lands in a DARK result box carrying the
   figure the whole calculation was built to produce. This is a ladder, NOT a
   chart: nothing here is scaled, because a derivation's steps are not commensurate
   (hours, percent and euro do not share an axis). Ref: Martic p6
   (5 x 160 = 800 Stunden, landing in "13.160 € pro Monat"); Frese p9
   (8 x 35,28 € x 210 = 133.358 €). #}
{% macro formula_ladder(v, uid=0) %}
{%- set schritte = (v.get('schritte') if v else none) or none -%}
{%- if schritte and (schritte | selectattr('wert') | list) -%}
{%- set ergebnis = v.get('ergebnis') or none -%}
<figure class="c-viz c-viz-ladder" role="img" aria-label="{% for s in schritte if s.wert %}{{ s.wert }} {{ s.einheit or '' }} {{ s.label or '' }}; {% endfor %}{% if ergebnis and ergebnis.wert %}{{ ergebnis.wert }} {{ ergebnis.label or '' }}{% endif %}">
  {%- if v.titel %}<figcaption class="c-viz-ladder__title" id="vizladder{{ uid }}">{{ v.titel }}</figcaption>{% endif -%}
  <ol class="c-viz-ladder__list">
  {%- for s in schritte if s.wert -%}
    <li class="c-viz-ladder__row">
      <span class="c-viz-ladder__chip">{{ loop.index }}</span>
      <span class="c-viz-ladder__figure">
        <span class="c-viz-ladder__wert">{{ s.wert }}</span>
        {%- if s.einheit %}<span class="c-viz-ladder__einheit">{{ s.einheit }}</span>{% endif -%}
      </span>
      {%- if s.label %}<span class="c-viz-ladder__label">{{ s.label }}</span>{% endif -%}
    </li>
  {%- endfor -%}
  </ol>
  {%- if ergebnis and ergebnis.wert -%}
  <div class="c-viz-ladder__ergebnis">
    <span class="c-viz-ladder__ergebnis-wert">{{ ergebnis.wert }}</span>
    {%- if ergebnis.label %}<span class="c-viz-ladder__ergebnis-label">{{ ergebnis.label }}</span>{% endif -%}
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if v.quelle %}<figcaption class="c-viz-ladder__source">{{ v.quelle }}</figcaption>{% endif -%}
</figure>
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{# grouped_bars (BEFORE/AFTER per CATEGORY). Per row: the category label, then two
   stacked horizontal bars, vorher in a muted context tone, nachher in solid
   accent, each carrying its value VERBATIM at the bar end. Both series share ONE
   scale (the max across every value in the table), which is what makes the pair
   comparable across rows. A legend beneath names the two series, using only the
   labels the writer supplied. Ref: Martic p9 (Reporting / Kampagnen-Setup /
   Werbemittel / Gesamt). #}
{% macro grouped_bars(v, uid=0) %}
{%- set zeilen = (v.get('zeilen') if v else none) or none -%}
{%- if zeilen and (zeilen | selectattr('label') | list) -%}
{%- set nums = (zeilen | map(attribute='vorher') | map('num') | list)
              + (zeilen | map(attribute='nachher') | map('num') | list) -%}
{%- set m = nums | max -%}
<figure class="c-viz c-viz-grouped" role="img" aria-label="{% for z in zeilen if z.label %}{{ z.label }}: {{ v.vorher_label or '' }} {{ z.vorher or '' }}, {{ v.nachher_label or '' }} {{ z.nachher or '' }}; {% endfor %}">
  {%- if v.titel %}<figcaption class="c-viz-grouped__title" id="vizgrouped{{ uid }}">{{ v.titel }}</figcaption>{% endif -%}
  <div class="c-viz-grouped__rows">
  {%- for z in zeilen if z.label -%}
    <div class="c-viz-grouped__row">
      <div class="c-viz-grouped__label">{{ z.label }}</div>
      <div class="c-viz-grouped__pair">
        {%- if z.vorher is defined and z.vorher -%}
        {%- set nv = z.vorher | num -%}
        {%- set wv = ((([((nv / m * 100) if m else 0) | round(0, 'floor') | int, 2] | max)) if nv > 0 else 0) -%}
        <div class="c-viz-grouped__track">
          <span class="c-viz-grouped__bar c-viz-grouped__bar--vorher" style="width:{{ wv }}%"></span>
          <span class="c-viz-grouped__val">{{ z.vorher }}{% if v.einheit %} {{ v.einheit }}{% endif %}</span>
        </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if z.nachher is defined and z.nachher -%}
        {%- set nn = z.nachher | num -%}
        {%- set wn = ((([((nn / m * 100) if m else 0) | round(0, 'floor') | int, 2] | max)) if nn > 0 else 0) -%}
        <div class="c-viz-grouped__track">
          <span class="c-viz-grouped__bar c-viz-grouped__bar--nachher" style="width:{{ wn }}%"></span>
          <span class="c-viz-grouped__val">{{ z.nachher }}{% if v.einheit %} {{ v.einheit }}{% endif %}</span>
        </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
  {%- if v.vorher_label or v.nachher_label -%}
  <div class="c-viz-grouped__legend">
    {%- if v.vorher_label -%}
    <span class="c-viz-grouped__leg"><span class="c-viz-grouped__swatch c-viz-grouped__swatch--vorher"></span>{{ v.vorher_label }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if v.nachher_label -%}
    <span class="c-viz-grouped__leg"><span class="c-viz-grouped__swatch c-viz-grouped__swatch--nachher"></span>{{ v.nachher_label }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if v.quelle %}<figcaption class="c-viz-grouped__source">{{ v.quelle }}</figcaption>{% endif -%}
</figure>
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{# stacked_bar_100 (COMPOSITION of a whole, and the before/after of ONE ratio).
   One full-width bar segmented by `teile`; each segment's width IS its percent, so
   the bar sums to exactly what the writer stated (nothing is normalised, nothing
   is padded to reach 100). A segment wide enough to hold its percent carries it
   INSIDE; a thin one carries it ABOVE, on a reserved lane, so a 1% sliver stays
   readable. The legend maps the tonal ramp back to the writer's labels.
   When `vergleich_teile` is present the device becomes TWO stacked bars, one per
   series, each named on the left by `teile_label` / `vergleich_label`, and the two
   share ONE ramp so a segment means the same thing in both rows. Ref: Frese p11
   (43/45/10/1); Martic p11 (87/13 vorher against 10/90 nachher). #}
{% macro stacked_bar_100(v, uid=0) %}
{%- set teile = (v.get('teile') if v else none) or none -%}
{%- if teile -%}
{%- set vergleich = (v.get('vergleich_teile') if v else none) or none -%}
{%- set reihen = [{'teile': teile, 'label': v.get('teile_label')}]
                 + ([{'teile': vergleich, 'label': v.get('vergleich_label')}] if vergleich else []) -%}
{# a percent under 8 cannot hold its own label inside the segment, so the whole
   device reserves an outside lane above the bars (uniformly, to keep the two
   series baselines aligned). #}
{%- set alle = teile + (vergleich or []) -%}
{%- set schmal = alle | map(attribute='prozent') | map('num') | select('lt', 8) | list -%}
<figure class="c-viz c-viz-stack{% if schmal %} c-viz-stack--outside{% endif %}" role="img" aria-label="{% for r in reihen %}{{ r.label or '' }} {% for t in r.teile %}{{ t.prozent }}% {{ t.label or '' }}; {% endfor %}{% endfor %}">
  {%- if v.titel %}<figcaption class="c-viz-stack__title" id="vizstack{{ uid }}">{{ v.titel }}</figcaption>{% endif -%}
  <div class="c-viz-stack__lines">
  {%- for r in reihen -%}
    <div class="c-viz-stack__line">
      {%- if r.label %}<span class="c-viz-stack__rowlabel">{{ r.label }}</span>{% endif -%}
      <span class="c-viz-stack__track">
        {%- for t in r.teile -%}
        {%- set p = t.prozent | num -%}
        {# the width IS the stated percent; a whole number stays whole (43, not
           43.0) so the geometry never invents a precision the writer did not. #}
        {%- set pw = (p | int) if (p == (p | round(0))) else (p | round(2)) -%}
        {%- set ptxt = (t.prozent | string) if ('%' in (t.prozent | string)) else ((t.prozent | string) ~ '%') -%}
        <span class="c-viz-stack__seg c-viz-stack__seg--t{{ (loop.index0 % 5) + 1 }}" style="width:{{ pw }}%">
          {%- if p >= 8 -%}
          <span class="c-viz-stack__pct">{{ ptxt }}</span>
          {%- elif p > 0 -%}
          <span class="c-viz-stack__pct c-viz-stack__pct--outside">{{ ptxt }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </span>
    </div>
  {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
  {%- if teile | selectattr('label') | list -%}
  <div class="c-viz-stack__legend">
    {%- for t in teile -%}{%- if t.label -%}
    <span class="c-viz-stack__leg"><span class="c-viz-stack__swatch c-viz-stack__swatch--t{{ (loop.index0 % 5) + 1 }}"></span>{{ t.label }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if v.quelle %}<figcaption class="c-viz-stack__source">{{ v.quelle }}</figcaption>{% endif -%}
</figure>
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{# entity_bars (ENTITIES compared on ONE metric). Per row: an optional `marke` (a
   SHORT text mark, e.g. a country name or code, rendered as a pill, never an emoji
   flag, which would not embed reliably in print), the entity name, then a bar
   carrying its value VERBATIM at the end. `wert` may be a RANGE ("3-5") or a
   German-formatted figure ("1.200", "2,5"): the bar length comes from the LEADING
   number, the label prints the string exactly as given, so a range is never
   re-rendered as a single number it does not claim. Bars share one scale (the max
   leading number across entries). Ref: Frese p11 (Ausbildungsdauer per country).
   #}
{% macro entity_bars(v, uid=0) %}
{%- set eintraege = (v.get('eintraege') if v else none) or none -%}
{%- if eintraege and (eintraege | selectattr('wert') | list) -%}
{%- set nums = eintraege | map(attribute='wert') | map('num') | list -%}
{%- set m = nums | max -%}
<figure class="c-viz c-viz-entity" role="img" aria-label="{% for e in eintraege if e.wert %}{{ e.name or '' }}: {{ e.wert }} {{ v.einheit or '' }}; {% endfor %}">
  {%- if v.titel %}<figcaption class="c-viz-entity__title" id="vizentity{{ uid }}">{{ v.titel }}</figcaption>{% endif -%}
  <ul class="c-viz-entity__list">
  {%- for e in eintraege if e.wert -%}
    {%- set n = e.wert | num -%}
    {%- set w = ((([((n / m * 100) if m else 0) | round(0, 'floor') | int, 2] | max)) if n > 0 else 0) -%}
    <li class="c-viz-entity__row">
      <span class="c-viz-entity__head">
        {%- if e.marke %}<span class="c-viz-entity__marke">{{ e.marke }}</span>{% endif -%}
        {%- if e.name %}<span class="c-viz-entity__name">{{ e.name }}</span>{% endif -%}
      </span>
      <span class="c-viz-entity__track">
        <span class="c-viz-entity__bar" style="width:{{ w }}%"></span>
        <span class="c-viz-entity__wert">{{ e.wert }}{% if v.einheit %} {{ v.einheit }}{% endif %}</span>
      </span>
    </li>
  {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>
  {%- if v.quelle %}<figcaption class="c-viz-entity__source">{{ v.quelle }}</figcaption>{% endif -%}
</figure>
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
